[ti:Between the Thorns and the Silk]
[ar:EdgarAllanMusic]
[al:Sidd-hartha.text - Reawakened]

[00:04.16]Yeah... from the fire to the feast... then the water calls
[00:13.10]Kamala taught the kiss... Kamaswami taught the cost
[00:21.12]First the thorns, the hunger
[00:23.12]Flesh denied and torn to shreds
[00:24.85]Starved the body raw
[00:25.92]Meditated till my mind bled
[00:27.76]Then flipped the script
[00:28.60]Silk robes, gold chains, nights of fire and storm
[00:31.79]Pleasure wrapped tight like a vice
[00:34.05]Golden chains keepin' me warm
[00:35.79]Lips like fresh figs, honey drippin', lost in the game
[00:38.79]Kamala smiled slow, said a samana can't love
[00:41.65]Had to drop the beggar rags, learn the city, rise above
[00:44.64]Ran from one extreme to the next like a fiend possessed by the flame
[00:48.74]Starved the flesh, fed the senses
[00:50.74]Still couldn't find no rest
[00:52.54]Till the current pulled a nigga in
[00:54.18]Slow, deep and wide, no contest
[00:56.94]The middle path... the river finds the way
[01:00.61](The middle path... the river finds the way)
[01:03.37]The middle path... the river finds the way
[01:06.12](The middle path... the river finds the way)
[01:08.52]Wealth became a second skin
[01:10.44]Desire became the air I breathe
[01:12.66]Heart grew heavy like concrete
[01:14.97]Soul forgot how to believe
[01:16.39]Kamaswami showed the ledgers, how the numbers turn to gold
[01:19.09]How to buy it cheap and sell it back before the story's told
[01:22.12]Merchants at the table, dice talkin' through the night
[01:24.92]Wine in the goblet, bets shinin' in the candlelight
[01:27.68]Every deal a little colder, every laugh a little thin
[01:30.78]I was winnin' like a man who couldn't feel the win
[01:33.00]Silk sheets, heavy pockets, people at my door
[01:35.40]Still that empty in the chest I been runnin' from before
[01:38.56]Taught me trade and title, how to smile and take my cut
[01:41.13]I learned the city language, then I learned to keep it shut
[01:43.96]Gambled till the morning, drank until the room would tilt
[01:46.72]Called it livin' large... it was just another kind of guilt
[01:51.35]The middle path... the river finds the way
[01:55.35](The middle path... the river finds the way)
[01:58.18]The middle path... the river finds the way
[02:00.87](The middle path... the river finds the way)
[02:03.06]Years went fat and hollow, mirrors wouldn't hold my face
[02:05.97]Kamala still beside me but the love had lost its taste
[02:08.67]That little bird I dreamed about was dyin' in the gold
[02:11.12]I heard it from the inside, now the cage was takin' hold
[02:13.92]Nausea in the gut, dread sittin' on my name
[02:16.66]Rich man in the silk, but the soul forgot the flame
[02:19.24]I stood up from the banquet with nothin' left to claim
[02:21.88]Then the slow current called
[02:23.55]Endless flowin' sound in the dark
[02:25.29]Where the starvin' saint breaks down
[02:27.22]And the rich man hits the ground hard
[02:29.68]No more denial, no more excess flame burnin' my name
[02:32.73]Just the quiet current callin' out my name in the rain
[02:35.48]River taught the lesson that the extremes never could teach
[02:38.05]You gotta feel it all
[02:39.73]Then let that shit go for good, no cap, no breach
[02:43.77]The middle path... the river finds the way
[02:47.17](The middle path... the river finds the way)
[02:51.55]The middle path... the river finds the way
[02:52.66](The middle path... the river finds the way)
[02:54.56]Songbird in the golden cage, note by note it died
[02:57.35]I was sleepin' next to fortune with a funeral inside
[03:00.36]Woke up sick of silk, sick of perfume, sick of gain
[03:02.72]When the bird went quiet, I walked out in the rain
[03:06.69]Between the starvin' saint and the man who lost his name
[03:11.63]The ferryman just smiles, the water knows the truth
[03:16.35]Balance only comes when you learn to lose, nigga
[03:19.94](The middle path... the river finds the way)
[03:22.68](The middle path... the river finds the way)
[03:25.23]From the thorns to the silk... then the river calls
[03:30.82]The middle path... the river finds the way... yeah
[03:34.94]
